# Skill: Test Strategy

Purpose:
  Define how the SDDRA system executes, evaluates, and maintains tests.
  This skill governs test selection, execution workflow, and failure handling.
  It is the single source of truth for AI-driven test execution.

ID: SKILL-TEST-STRATEGY

Domain: testing

Level: L3

Status: STABLE

Use:
  - AI test execution
  - CI/CD test pipelines
  - Test impact analysis
  - Failure investigation

Input:
  - Task context (impact, risk, stack)
  - Project test state
  - Test type definitions
  - Gate criteria

Output:
  - Test execution plan
  - Selected test types
  - Pass/fail results
  - Failure findings

Execute:
  1. Receive task context from chain engine
  2. Query .sdd/testing/types.sdd for applicable test types
  3. Select tests based on impact and risk
  4. Execute .sdd/testing/scripts/run.ps1 with appropriate category
  5. Parse results and generate findings
  6. Update projects/vkard.az/testing/ state
  7. Route failures to task graph

Test Selection Rules:
  [TS1] Every task MUST have at least one unit test.
  [TS2] API changes MUST include contract tests.
  [TS3] Security changes MUST include security gate tests.
  [TS4] UI changes MUST include E2E tests.
  [TS5] Data changes MUST include integration tests.
  [TS6] Performance-critical paths MUST include performance tests.

Execution Rules:
  [TS7] Tests MUST be executed from .sdd/testing/scripts/.
  [TS8] AI MUST NOT create ad-hoc test commands outside this skill.
  [TS9] Test results MUST be stored in .sdd/projects/vkard.az/testing/.
  [TS10] Flaky tests MUST be quarantined and investigated.

State: +
